Title: M54-M6 link road 'could generate more than £500m' for UK economy
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Lee Carter', 'Text': 'Telford and Wrekin Council leader Lee Carter said the "landmark" project was expected to generate between £555m and £634m in economic benefits', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 118}}, {'Speaker': 'Lee Carter', 'Text': 'He said it could also cut journey times for commuters, remove about 19,000 drivers from nearby roads and improve access to jobs.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 106}}, {'Speaker': 'Lee Carter', 'Text': '"This important link is about making life easier for working people, attracting new investment, and ensuring Telford remains a key player in the Midlands economy," the Labour leader said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 172}}, {'Speaker': 'Lee Carter', 'Text': '"Seeing this connection move forward is a significant and welcome step for our community."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 75}}, {'Speaker': 'Lee Carter', 'Text': 'He told BBC Radio Shropshire that, while the construction phase would inconvenience people, it would "make life a lot easier" once it was finished.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 128}}, {'Speaker': 'Richard Parker', 'Text': 'West Midlands mayor Richard Parker said it would provide faster journeys and improve connections for "thousands of people and businesses" in the Black Country and surrounding areas.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 170}}, {'Speaker': 'Richard Parker', 'Text': '"This will transform the region, drive growth and opportunity in every community - and help us deliver better journeys for everyone," he said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 123}}, {'Speaker': 'Sir Gavin Williamson', 'Text': 'Sir Gavin Williamson, Conservative MP for Stone, Great Wyrley and Penkridge, said it would make a "real difference" to communities.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 108}}, {'Speaker': 'Sir Gavin Williamson', 'Text': '"Residents in Featherstone, Hilton, and Shareshill have had to deal with increased congestion in their villages and difficulties with access," he added.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}, {'Speaker': 'Mark Pritchard', 'Text': '"It cannot mean a new road comes at any cost to local villages and communities," he told BBC Radio Shropshire.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}, {'Speaker': 'Mark Pritchard', 'Text': '"The downside potentially is this creeping urbanisation – light industrialisation – of the east of our county."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Speaker': 'Mark Pritchard', 'Text': 'The Conservative representative said Shropshire was a "growing county" but it needed to grow in a way so as to protect its green spaces.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 115}}, {'Speaker': 'Chancellor Rachel Reeves', 'Text': '"These vital investments are long overdue, will transform local communities and improve living standards across the country," said Chancellor Rachel Reeves.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}], 'Description': [], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "A woman with curly dark brown hair, nearly to her shoulders, sits in a car's driving seat, hands on the wheel, wearing a light green top. The car is light green too."}]}
